From a0c9be95e797640fb65edae8bb4ecf7cb0b9d121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 05:26:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] The rack as an instrument, and the way in for everyone
 else
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S1–S7, A1, A3, A4, A6, A7.

Sound
  The bypass can be level-matched. Louder wins every blind comparison
  ever run, so a rack with make-up gain always sounds better and you
  never hear what it is doing — the match measures the difference and
  applies it to the quieter leg, beside the honest hard bypass rather
  than instead of it.

  What it measures took two goes. Comparing the signal entering the rack
  with the signal leaving it is wrong: a bypass is not the dry input, it
  is the same chain with its settings neutralised, and the width matrix,
  the wet/dry sum and the limiter all have a gain of their own. Measured,
  the rack made a record 1.1 dB quieter than its own bypass while the
  first correction moved it 2.8 dB the other way. It now measures the
  rack's transfer function with the rack in, then again with it out, and
  takes the difference of the two ratios — which divides the music out,
  so two readings a second apart can be compared at all.

  Two racks, A and B, one key to swap. A momentary mono check, held from
  the keyboard or from the button: the width control already reached
  mono, but as a setting you had to remember to put back, which is not
  how anybody checks anything.

  A correlation meter under the VU, fed by three more sums over the 128
  floats the meter worklet had already walked — no second tap. Level is
  the one thing a listener can already judge; phase is what tells you a
  record will collapse on a phone speaker.

  Numbers on the spectrum: a live plot behind the curve, a dBFS scale, a
  peak hold, and a readout under the pointer. Read from a new plain
  `spectrum()` rather than `analysis()`, whose bands are tilted, curved
  and normalised for the eye — a dB scale against those would be a ruler
  beside a lie.

  A rack as a file, written out and read back, with everything in the
  file bounded on the way in and what it would change shown before it
  changes anything.

  And a phase vocoder, behind a quality setting that says what it costs:
  50 ms of latency and two FFTs a hop, against a delay line that costs
  neither and warbles past about seven semitones. Verified against a
  440 Hz tone: +12 gives 894 Hz, −12 gives 226 Hz, and both shifters now
  agree on level to within a fifth of a decibel — the overlap-add
  normalisation had been fixed at the unity hop, which cost 3 dB at +7
  and gained about as much going down.

Reach
  The two muted ink tokens measured 3.83:1 and 3.54:1 against this
  application's own background, where AA asks 4.5:1 below 18.66px — and
  essentially every use of them is 9 to 12.5px. Lifted to 10.2:1 and
  7.0:1, mirrored in light.

  A skip link, because every route puts ten navigation items before the
  content. One focus-ring floor for everything interactive, as an
  outline rather than a shadow: half the controls here are cut with
  clip-path chamfers, and a shadow is clipped away with the corner.

  Shortcuts can be remapped by pressing them, which the keyboard table
  made nearly free — and `conflicts()` now compares against what each
  binding currently answers to rather than what it was declared with,
  which had it reporting the opposite of the truth once anything had
  been moved.

  The Circle Analysis Center is a hand-packed SVG: a picture of numbers a
  screen reader is handed as one line of alt text. The same figures are
  now a table, with a search, offered to everybody. Past thirty-two the
  tail is drawn as one circle that says how many it stands for and opens
  the table — a chart that silently drops its long tail claims the total
  it shows is the whole total.

Also: layout.mjs called the skip link unreachable, which it is not — a
control that parks off screen and returns on focus is the opposite. The
tool now checks by focusing it, with the transition suppressed for the
measurement, because reading it a microtask later caught it mid-flight
and failed at one width out of six.

